		{
			"id": "t3y-ucuIDJqC-vKsS",
			"name": "Devourer",
			"reference": "B61",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A heavier gun-arm that hurls squirming, burrowing worms deep into a wound at automatic-weapon speed, favoured by Tyranid Warriors and Hive Tyrants who want sustained close-range firepower rather than a single hard-hitting shot. Codex: Tyranids background places it a clear step above the Fleshborer/Spinefists family and roughly level with an Astra Militarum autogun in raw stopping power, made up for by its far higher rate of fire.\n\nDesign: Framework.md's own anchor (updated after flak went to DR 30, for the same reason as the Fleshborer above): \"Devourer | Boring worms: 5d(2) pi++.\" Innate Attack (Huge Pierce) (B61, 8/die) at 5 dice = 40, with Armor Divisor (2) (B102, +50%) and Rapid Fire (B105, RoF 5-8 bracket, +70%): net +120%, 40x2.2=88. Checked by exact dice distribution: 5d(2) pi++ averages 17.5 and penetrates flak (DR 30, eff. 15) 69.5% of the time and rounds to 0% against carapace (DR 70, eff. 35) or heavier — now a genuinely reliable threat to flak-armoured infantry per shot, well past the old 4d(2) figure's 33.6% and past even the framework's own autogun anchor (9% vs flak), matching a \"boring worms\" weapon meant to chew through soft armour outright; RoF 8 then stacks on top of that already-solid per-shot chance, making a Warrior's Devourer a serious threat to anything short of carapace. Handling: Acc 3 and 150/450 range, this project's own rifle-class estimate for a Warrior-scale gun-arm; Shots 12(20), a shorter, 20-second regrowth for the faster-cycling brood.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Xenos",
				"Tyranids"
			],
			"base_points": 88,
			"weapons": [
				{
					"id": "WmbjzQhtrh8JwVfn8",
					"sv": 1,
					"damage": {
						"type": "pi++",
						"base": "5d",
						"armor_divisor": 2
					},
					"accuracy": "3",
					"range": "150/450",
					"rate_of_fire": "8",
					"shots": "12(20)",
					"usage": "Standard",
					"usage_notes": "ST-independent, fused to the arm. Shots regrow from the bearer's boring-worm glands over the listed time.",
					"defaults": [
						{
							"type": "skill",
							"name": {
								"compare": "is",
								"qualifier": "Innate Attack"
							},
							"specialization": {
								"compare": "is",
								"qualifier": "Projectile"
							}
						},
						{
							"type": "dx",
							"modifier": -4
						}
					]
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "t_YrkYJmbDmbhGeQJ",
			"name": "Bonesword",
			"reference": "B88",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A blade of psychically-hardened bone, carried by Tyranid Warriors and Primes and charged with a disruptive field the Hive Mind itself sustains — the swarm's own answer to a power weapon, shearing through armour a plain scything talon or rending claw cannot touch. Codex: Tyranids background places boneswords firmly in the same armour-shredding tier as an Astartes power sword, usually wielded alongside a Lash Whip that pins a target still for the killing blow.\n\nDesign: Framework.md's own anchor: \"Bonesword | Psychically charged bone blade: sw+3d(10) cut (power-field class).\" Built at a Tyranid Warrior's own ST 24 (sw 4d+2): Cutting Striker (B88, 7 points) with Armor Divisor (10) (B102, +200%) = 21 for the sw+0(10) baseline; the anchor's own +3d is bought as Innate Attack (Cut) (B61, 7/die) at 3 dice = 21, with Armor Divisor (10) (+200%) and Melee Attack, Reach C (-30%): net +170%, 21x2.7=56.7, rounded to 57. Total 21+57=78 — priced in the same tier as this project's Custodes power weapons for the same reason: a divisor-(10) weapon is always expensive to buy as a character trait, whatever grows or forges it. Checked by exact dice distribution at ST 24 (sw+3d(10) = 7d+2(10)): averages 26.5 and clears every personal-armour DR at 100%, including Astartes plate (DR 100, eff. 10) at 100%, and a Terminator (DR 200, eff. 20) at 90.6% — a genuine Marine-and-near-Terminator killer, matching \"same armour-shredding tier as a power sword\" (framework's own power sword anchor, sw+3d+1(10), sits almost exactly here) without exceeding it.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Xenos",
				"Tyranids"
			],
			"base_points": 78,
			"weapons": [
				{
					"id": "wL0ymDEYLlKbFsM2u",
					"sv": 1,
					"damage": {
						"type": "cut",
						"st": "sw",
						"base": "3d",
						"armor_divisor": 10
					},
					"reach": "1",
					"parry": "0",
					"usage": "Standard",
					"usage_notes": "Written for a Tyranid Warrior/Prime-scale bearer (ST 24, sw 4d+2, giving a total of 7d+2(10) cut); rebuild the +3d Innate Attack component for any other bearer's own ST per this file's header note.",
					"defaults": [
						{
							"type": "dx",
							"modifier": 0
						},
						{
							"type": "skill",
							"name": {
								"compare": "is",
								"qualifier": "Brawling"
							}
						}
					]
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "tz_Ebiioh7TVRBXf1",
			"name": "Lash Whip",
			"reference": "B41",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A long, muscular, whip-like limb almost always carried alongside a Bonesword: not primarily a killing weapon, but a control one, lashing out to entangle and unbalance a target so the blade in the creature's other limb can land a clean, undefended blow. Codex: Tyranids background is explicit that Lash Whip and Bonesword are a matched pair on Tyranid Warriors and Primes, one pinning while the other kills.\n\nDesign: No framework anchor gives this weapon exact numbers, only its control-weapon role, so it is built directly on that role: Binding (B41, 2 points/level) at level 20, matching a Tyranid Warrior/Prime's own ST 24 minus some slack for the whip's own flexibility versus a solid limb's grip = 40 points, plus a minor Crushing Striker (B88, 5 points) with the Long 1 enhancement for its extra reach (this project's own estimated +40%/level, since Basic Set's core rules don't tabulate a Claws/Striker reach extension and this project's Necron/Ork files already document similar own-estimate percentages for un-tabled Basic Set options): 5x1.4=7. Total 40+7=47. No exact- dice penetration check applies to a Binding-based control weapon in the way it does to a damage-dealing one; its function is to set up the Bonesword's own (10)-divisor hit, not to punch through armour itself. Reach 1-2 and Parry -1 reflect a long, flexible limb that reaches further than a talon but is a worse parrying tool for it.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Xenos",
				"Tyranids"
			],
			"base_points": 47,
			"weapons": [
				{
					"id": "wMeAfxIsTFDvI1i8i",
					"sv": 1,
					"damage": {
						"type": "cr"
					},
					"reach": "1,2",
					"parry": "-1",
					"usage": "Standard (entangle)",
					"usage_notes": "Binding 20 (B41): a successful hit entangles rather than damages by default; the target must beat the Lash Whip's own Binding 20 (as an effective ST/DX contest per B41) to break free before its bearer's Bonesword or Scything Talons finish the job. The listed cr damage is what a Lash Whip does if its bearer chooses to lash rather than bind on a given hit.",
